.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt CURL 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm curl
.Nd simple HTTP and verified HTTPS fetch
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl I
.Op Fl L
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl -max-time Ar seconds
.Op Fl H Ar "Name: value"
.Op Fl -cacert Ar file
.Ar URL
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility performs one bounded HTTP GET for
.Ar URL .
The response body is written to standard output unless
.Fl o
selects a file.
.Pp
The base build is plain HTTP over
.Xr raven-http 3
and
.Xr raven-http-net 3 .
It does not link C or OpenSSL; an
.Pa https://
URL fails with a clear
.Dv EUNAVAILABLE
message instead of downloading without verification.
The optional TLS add-on build links
.Xr raven-tls 3
and the owner-approved OpenSSL add-on; it verifies the certificate chain and
the host name or IP address and never falls back to an unverified connection.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o Ar file
Write the response body to
.Ar file .
The value
.Sq -
means standard output.
An existing file is overwritten.
.It Fl s
Suppress non-body diagnostics.
.It Fl f
Treat an HTTP status of 400 or greater as failure.
.It Fl I
Print the status line and headers.
This is a GET whose body is discarded; there is no HEAD method.
.It Fl L
Follow up to five redirects.
Without this option the redirect budget is zero.
.It Fl -max-time Ar seconds
Set the total request deadline in seconds.
The default is 10.
.It Fl H Ar "Name: value"
Add one request header.
Reserved hop-by-hop and host headers are rejected.
.It Fl -cacert Ar file
TLS add-on build only: trust exactly this PEM bundle instead of the default
.Pa /addons/etc/ssl/certs/ca-bundle.pem .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 2; an HTTP failure selected by
.Fl f
exits with status 22.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wget 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
This is a deliberately small subset, not a GNU curl replacement.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.0.
